# The road home, once per save, the first night the caravan rests with
# two or more regalia pieces aboard (WorldComponent_TSC_RegaliaRoad).
# A remnant of the Baron's people, come to sell the king's waking back
# to the company. Pay, talk, or steel - steel is a real ambush.

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_RegaliaRoad

== start ==
Hooves, walking pace, deliberate: riders who want to be heard coming. Four of them stop at the edge of the firelight and the front one leans on his saddle horn.

"Evening. You are the company off the barrow road, carrying what you are carrying. We rode for the Baron, when there was a Baron. We know what dead kings' trinkets fetch, and we know who is buying. So: toll. Two hundred silver, and the road east is yours, and nobody has to bleed."

* "Two hundred, and you were never here." -> paid
    if has_item(Silver, 200)
* "You rode for the Baron. You saw what sleeping next to one piece did to him. We are carrying the makings of the man it *obeyed*. Ride away."
    check Persuasion 11 -> ride_off | insulted
* [Say nothing. Stand up.] -> steel

== paid ==
The silver goes into a saddlebag without being counted.

"Wise," the rider says, turning his horse. "The Baron counted his. Every night. You saw how he ended." They are gone at a walk, unhurried, the way they came.

* [Let them go.] -> end
    do take_item(Silver, 200)

== ride_off ==
The rider does not answer at once, and behind him a horse shifts as its man's hands go quiet on the reins.

"We did see," the rider says at last. All the market-stall ease is gone. "Five years of watching him count. You are right, and I am cold, and this was a bad idea I owed the boys an attempt at."

He straightens up. "Keep the toll. Ride careful. Whatever you wake at the end of this road, tell it the Baron's men are done."

* [Let them go.] -> end
    do grant_xp(80)

== insulted ==
The rider does not answer at once, and behind him a horse shifts as its man's hands go quiet on the reins.

"The Baron," the rider says, quietly, "fed us for five years, and went mad doing it, and you will not lecture me about him at your own fire."

He wheels the horse. "Take them, and take the trinkets."

* [Steel.] -> steel

== steel ==
The riders come out of the dark in earnest.

* [Meet them.] -> end
    do ambush_caravan()
